# Billing and paywall

PocketHost is a **hard paywall** hosting service. There is **no free hosting tier** and no freemium plan for new customers.

## Target model: Pay Per PocketBase (Jul 2026)

Per instance:

| Billing | Price |
| ------- | ----- |
| Monthly | **$9.99**/instance (7-day trial) |
| Annual | **$59.99**/instance (~50% vs 12× monthly) |
| Lifetime | **$149.99**/instance |

Each paid instance (`subscription_quantity`) adds:

- **One more instance.** You can have as many instances as you pay for, and all of them can run. Powered-off instances still count. There is **no powered-on cap** and no "unlimited instance records" (that older model was dropped).
- **10 GB** of pooled **disk storage**: everything on our servers (databases, logs, `pb_public`, hooks, backups, local uploads). Files in the customer's own S3 bucket don't count.

Legacy plans with 250+ instances (Flounder, Founder, retired "unlimited" plans) get a **flat 25 GB** of disk storage, not 10 GB × instances. Accounts with no paid instances get **1 GB**. Policy text lives in `/docs/limits#disk-storage`. It is published policy only. Nothing in code meters or enforces it.

Checkout quantity = number of instances.

**No Pro, Agency, or tiered plans.** One product: Pay Per PocketBase with three billing intervals.

**Grandfathered** accounts (Legacy, Flounder, Founder, early `subscription=free` rows, etc.) keep prior entitlements until migrated. **Jul 1, 2026:** new price points for **new purchases only**. Existing accounts unchanged.

**`users.subscription === 'free'`** in mothership is a **legacy DB enum value**, not a product tier.

## Checkout (live Jul 2026)

Dashboard `/pricing` and Lemon Squeezy checkout use **$9.99/mo**, **$59.99/yr**, and **$149.99 lifetime** per instance. **Annual** is the featured interval on `/pricing` (~50% savings vs 12 months of monthly). Legacy $5/mo and $359 Flounder are off checkout. Grandfathered webhook mappings remain for existing rows.

## Copy rules for agents

**Do not write:**

- "free tier", "Free plan", "Hacker tier", Pro/Agency tiers, or tier comparison tables with $19.99/$49.99
- "paid plans" vs "free tier" for standard features
- "Pro subscribers" (use **subscribers** or **Pay Per PocketBase**)
- Em dashes (`—`) in customer-facing copy. Use a period and a new sentence, or rewrite. See [communication-style.mdc](communication-style.mdc).

**Do write:**

- **Pay Per PocketBase**, **$9.99/mo**, **$59.99/yr**, **$149.99 lifetime** per instance (LS list prices), **disk storage**
- Annual savings vs monthly when comparing intervals (~$60/instance/year, ~50%)
- "subscribe", "your account", "add another instance". Say "instances", never "slots" or "PocketBases" (see [end-user-docs.mdc](end-user-docs.mdc))
- "grandfathered" for pre-paywall or legacy rows
- Third-party free tiers OK (Web Awesome, npm, etc.)

## Code

- `SubscriptionType.Premium` / `'premium'` = active Pay Per PocketBase subscriber (monthly or annual; DB enum name is historical).
- `subscription_interval`: `month`, `year`, or `life` (lifetime / legacy Flounder).
- `subscription_quantity` = paid instance count. The dashboard caps total instances at it. The edge daemon refuses to run instances when it is 0.
- `common/subscriptionLimits.ts` still has the old DB/file split constants for the account page meters. They predate the disk storage policy and nothing populates usage.
- Feature gates: prefer active hosting entitlement, not bare `subscription !== 'free'`, unless blocking lapsed accounts only.

Read [MEMORY.md](MEMORY.md) Billing section when touching pricing, limits, dashboard paywalls, or Lemon Squeezy flows.
